# Audio, labels and anything cut from a recording. Prod turns are real people's
# voices and their Scribe transcripts; public corpora carry licences that forbid
# redistribution (CV, L2-ARCTIC, ESC-50 are NC or click-through). All of it is
# re-creatable by scripts/prepare_*.py from sources the README names.
data/
# Downloaded and exported model weights.
models/
# A --limit run is a smoke test, never a result; it is kept out of git so it can
# never be mistaken for one.
results/smoke/
# Scores and replay logs of prod-derived tags, even when the ids are opaque:
# per-turn timing plus a language is enough to re-identify a short session.
results/private/
results/**/*.wav
# esbuild output of the real SpeechGate.
.cache/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# Per-row outputs (~4 MB of scores per run; facts carry speaker embeddings once
# sessions are in) and the run's manifest copy. `git rm` never shrinks history,
# so only what a gate is argued from is tracked: summary.json/.md, gate.json,
# <arm>.model.json, <arm>.meta.json, <arm>.parity.json, run.json. All per-row
# files are re-derivable by re-running the tag.
results/**/*.scores.jsonl
# A half-written score file of an interrupted arm, kept so the run resumes.
results/**/*.scores.partial.jsonl
results/**/facts.jsonl
results/**/manifest.jsonl
# Per-turn language tags are scores in all but name.
results/**/sensevoice_lid.jsonl
# Checkpoints SpeechBrain copies next to an arm.
arms/*/pretrained/
